Title: "Overview"
Id: "4f8cf47d-3b81-45db-8104-f888b3cc3ada"

Text: "```mlg-fragment
TopLevelItemUnion ::=
    | TitleGroup
    | SectionTitleGroup
    | SubsectionTitleGroup
    | TextGroup
    | TopLevelWritingGroup
    | DisambiguatesGroup
    | DeclaresGroup
    | DefinesGroup
    | RealizesGroup
    | RefinesGroup
    | StatesGroup
    | AxiomGroup
    | TheoremGroup
    | ConjectureGroup
    | PersonGroup
    | ResourceGroup
    | SpecifyGroup
    | RelationGroup
    | EquivalentGroup
    | TopicGroup
    | TextItemGroup
```

The group kind is determined by the first section label, never by the heading.
Every top-level item additionally accepts a final optional `Id:` section holding
a quoted UUID; `mlg check` adds a missing one, and duplicate ids are errors.

Groups with command headings introduce command signatures: `Declares:`,
`Defines:`, `Realizes:`, `Refines:`, `States:`, `Equivalent:`, and the theorem-like groups
that carry an optional heading. Duplicate signatures are rejected across all of
these kinds.

Every non-prose top-level item (`Declares:`, `Defines:`, `Realizes:`, `Refines:`, `States:`,
`Axiom:`, `Theorem:`, `Conjecture:`, `Relation:`, and `Disambiguates:`) may
carry its own optional `Writing:` section immediately after `Aliases:`.

`Declares:` defines reusable types and interfaces. `Defines:` introduces typed
values and operations, and may use `abstractly:` when a later `Realizes:` item
will supply its open components. `Realizes:` provides a concrete implementation
of one such abstract definition.

`Corollary:`, `Lemma:`, `Represents:`, and `Subsubsection:` are not part of the
structural language. `Conjecture:` and the opaque `Text…:` placeholders are
available for unproved or intentionally unstructured content."
Id: "0458cfe8-4b85-4c0f-8fbb-7d78e5cb80f5"
